  "issue_number": 3472,
  "issue_title": "Add a network emission-yield summary alongside the decentralization scorecard",
  "issue_body": "## Context\n\n`GET /api/v1/chain/yield` is real and live today: `src/chain-yield.mjs` (`buildChainYield`/`loadChainYield`), documented in `src/contracts.mjs:1372-1373` and exposed as an MCP tool `get_chain_yield` in `src/mcp-server.mjs:2511-2519`. It returns a network-wide emission-yield aggregate \u2014 the return-rate companion to `/chain/performance` \u2014 computed live from the `neurons` D1 tier, with no static-file fallback. The frontend has no idea it exists: no query function, no type, no route or component reads it anywhere in `apps/ui/src`.\n\n## Requirement\n\nRender a network emission-yield summary \u2014 the aggregate network return split by validator/miner role plus its percentile spread \u2014 as its own section, placed directly alongside (or inside) the network decentralization scorecard this issue is scoped to pair with (#3471).\n\n## Backend\n\n- Endpoint: `GET /api/v1/chain/yield`\n- Response shape (from `buildChainYield()` in `src/chain-yield.mjs:191-211`): `schema_version`, `subnet_count`, `neuron_count`, `validator_count`, `miner_count`, `captured_at`, `total_stake_tao`, `total_emission_tao`, `network_yield` (aggregate return = total emission / total stake, null when no neuron has stake+emission), `validator_yield`, `miner_yield` (same split by role), and `distribution` (nullable: `count`, `mean`, `median`, `min`, `max`, `p10`, `p25`, `p75`, `p90` over every neuron's individual emission/stake return).\n- Query function: **none exists.** `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/queries.ts` has the sibling pattern already in place for the two related network-wide artifacts \u2014 `chainConcentrationQuery` (`queries.ts:3684-3698`) and `chainPerformanceQuery` (`queries.ts:3701-3715`) \u2014 but no `chainYieldQuery`. Likewise `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/types.ts` defines `ChainConcentration` (`types.ts:1662-1674`) and `ChainPerformance` (`types.ts:1677-1689`) but no `ChainYield`. This PR must add both the `ChainYield` type (`types.ts`) and a `chainYieldQuery` + `normalizeChainYield` pair (`queries.ts`), following the exact `queryOptions`/`apiFetch`/normalize shape those two neighbors use, **as well as** the UI wiring in the same PR \u2014 a data-layer-only PR is exactly the failure mode this rewrite exists to prevent.\n\n## Deliverable\n\n- Files to change: `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/types.ts` (add `ChainYield` interface), `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/queries.ts` (add `normalizeChainYield` + `chainYieldQuery`, mirroring `normalizeChainConcentration`/`chainConcentrationQuery` at `queries.ts:3481-3495` and `3684-3698`), plus a route/component under `apps/ui/src/routes/` or `apps/ui/src/components/metagraphed/` to render it.\n- Exact anchor: there is no `/network` route yet, and #3471's decentralization scorecard (the stated pairing target) is itself unbuilt \u2014 `chainConcentrationQuery`/`chainPerformanceQuery` are only exercised today by `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/queries.chain-decentralization.test.ts`, never mounted in a component. This issue's job is the yield half only: add the query/type, then render a self-contained yield summary section that #3471's PR (or a follow-up wiring pass) can sit beside on whatever page/route that scorecard lands on \u2014 do not build the `/network` page itself here, that's #3471's job. If #3471 has already landed a page shell by the time this is picked up, extend that page's `SectionHeading` list instead of introducing a second route.\n- What to render: a `StatTile` row (`apps/ui/src/components/metagraphed/charts/stat-tile.tsx` \u2014 icon/eyebrow/value/hint/tone props, already used for compact KPI strips) with three tiles \u2014 Network yield (`network_yield`), Validator yield (`validator_yield`), Miner yield (`miner_yield`) \u2014 each formatted as a percentage/rate with `captured_at` as the shared hint, plus a percentile-spread readout (p10/p25/median/p75/p90 from `distribution`) underneath, e.g. as a compact table or inline stat strip. Render nothing (fall through to the empty state) when `network_yield` is null.\n- Coordination note: this is the yield twin of #3471 (decentralization scorecard, `/chain/concentration` + `/chain/performance`) \u2014 same \"pairs with\" relationship the parent issue names. Two separate PRs will likely touch the same target page/section list; keep this PR's rendered output as an independent section so it composes cleanly regardless of merge order. Also distinct from #3478 (per-subnet yield tab, `/subnets/{netuid}/yield`) \u2014 that is a different endpoint and a different page; do not conflate the two or reuse one PR for both.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Diff touches at least one file under `apps/ui/src/routes/` or `apps/ui/src/components/` (not just `queries.ts`/`types.ts`)\n- [ ] `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/queries.ts` gains a `chainYieldQuery` and `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/types.ts` gains a `ChainYield` type, both following the existing `chainConcentrationQuery`/`ChainConcentration` pattern\n- [ ] The component imports and calls `chainYieldQuery` via `useQuery`/`useSuspenseQuery`\n- [ ] Renders `network_yield`, `validator_yield`, and `miner_yield` as distinct labeled values, plus the `distribution` percentile spread (at minimum median + p10/p90)\n- [ ] `captured_at` is shown as a freshness/as-of hint somewhere in the section\n- [ ] Loading + empty + error states handled, matching the `Suspense`/`QueryErrorBoundary`/`Skeleton` fallback + `EmptyState` convention already used in `apps/ui/src/routes/status.tsx`\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Building the `/network` (or wherever-it-lands) page shell itself \u2014 that's #3471's scope; this issue only needs to produce a section/component ready to sit inside it\n- Per-subnet yield (`/subnets/{netuid}/yield`, #3478) \u2014 different endpoint, different page, not this PR\n- Any historical/trend view of network yield \u2014 `/api/v1/chain/yield` is a snapshot-only endpoint with no `/history` sibling; do not invent one\n\n## Size\n\nSize: S \u2014 keep this PR small (aim for \u226410 files / \u22641000 LOC).\n\nPart of #2542.",
